## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant QoS with dynamic config in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Traefik RateLimit middleware, Redis store, per-tenant quotas, Docker Config
- TLS termination, hot-reload without restart, cross-DC coordination
- Request tagging with X-Tenant and validation of isolation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo middleware sketch: extract tenant and enforce quota from Redis
async function enforceTenantRate(req, res, next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  const quota = await redisGetQuota(tenant);
  if (quota.allow(req)) return next();
  res.status(429).send('Too Many Requests');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you audit cross-DC quota drift and recover from Redis replication lag?
- How would you test hot-reload behavior under config churn?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates practical skills in dynamic per-tenant API version routing, assessing candidates' knowledge of Redis-backed routing state, Traefik dynamic configuration, and Docker-based edge proxies across distributed infrastructure.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant version routing
- Redis-backed configuration store (tenant_id → api_version)
- Traefik dynamic configuration via Docker provider
- Sidecar pattern for pushing configuration updates
- Multi-datacenter consistency and TLS edge handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Sidecar that watches Redis and updates Traefik rules
async function syncRoutes(redis, docker) {
  const routes = await redis.hgetall('tenant:versions');
  for (const [tenantId, version] of Object.entries(routes)) {
    await updateTraefikRule(docker, tenantId, version);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to add non-intrusive QA in production, teaches traffic manipulation without risking user impact, and validates multi-DC deployment awareness.

## Key Concepts
- Traffic shadowing vs canary releases
- Nginx mirror and upstream configuration
- Docker-DC/edge proxy routing across DCs
- TLS edge termination and tenant isolation

## Code Example
```nginx
# Example shadow config snippet
upstream prod_api { server prod-api:8080; }
upstream staging_api { server staging-api:8080; }
server {
  listen 443 ssl;
  location /api/ {
    proxy_pass http://prod_api;
    mirror /mirror_to_staging;
  }
  location = /mirror_to_staging {
    proxy_pass http://staging_api;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor shadowed traffic to ensure no unseen side effects?
- How would you prevent skew if tenant_id headers can be spoofed?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical knowledge of per-tenant configuration via Docker Config, feature gating, and edge proxy routing in a multi-DC setup.

## Key Concepts
- Docker Config for per-tenant rules
- Feature flag gating in API
- Traefik TLS and docker-dca wiring
- Lightweight bootstrap and config reload

## Code Example
```javascript
// sample Express middleware for feature gate
const fs = require('fs');
let flags = {};
try { flags = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('/config/feature-flags.json','utf8')); } catch(e) { flags = {}; }
function featureGate(req,res,next){
  const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
  if(!tenant) return res.status(400).send('Missing X-Tenant');
  const enabled = flags[tenant] && flags[tenant].includes('new-feature');
  if(!enabled) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
app.get('/new-feature', featureGate, (req,res)=>{ res.send('New feature access granted'); });
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you hot-reload the flags without restarting the API?
- How would you test isolation across tenants when flags change?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design dynamic, per-tenant tracing in a multi-DC docker-dca setup, including config retrieval, TTL-based caching, and graceful degradation when the sidecar cannot fetch config.

## Key Concepts
- OpenTelemetry sampling and per-tenant configuration
- Consul KV as a central per-tenant policy store
- TTL caching to limit external calls
- Graceful fallback to sensible default rate
- Cross-DC deployment considerations and observability impact

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-sampler for per-tenant tracing
class TenantSampler {
  constructor(fetchRate) {
    this.fetchRate = fetchRate; // function(tenant) -> rate
    this.cache = new Map(); // tenant -> {rate, expiry}
  }
  getRate(tenant) {
    const entry = this.cache.get(tenant);
    if (entry && entry.expiry > Date.now()) return entry.rate;
    // fetch from Consul KV here, then cache for 5s
    const rate = this.fetchRate(tenant) ?? 20;
    this.cache.set(tenant, { rate, expiry: Date.now() + 5000 });
    return rate;
  }
  shouldSample(tenant) {
    const rate = this.getRate(tenant);
    return Math.random() * 100 < rate;
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test correctness of per-tenant rates during rollout?
- What are failure modes if Consul KV is unavailable, and how to mitigate them?
